The latest version of NTL is available at http://www.shoup.net.


----------------------------------------------------------------
QUICK START
----------------------------------------------------------------

NTL 12.0 uses Meson + Ninja as its build system.  From the top of the
source tree:

   meson setup --prefix=$HOME/.local build
   meson compile -C build
   meson test -C build
   meson install -C build

The result: libntl + headers + ntl.pc under $HOME/.local.

For the full guide (cross-compile, GMP, GF2X, auto-tuning, supported
options) see:

   doc/build.txt            — primary build guide
   doc/wizard.txt           — auto-tuning Wizard (replaces TUNE=auto)

If you previously used `./configure && make` on NTL 11.x or earlier,
NTL 12.0 is BREAKING — that path no longer exists.  See:

   doc/migration-from-makefile.txt


----------------------------------------------------------------
BREAKING CHANGES IN NTL 12.0
----------------------------------------------------------------

   *  The Perl `./configure` + Makefile + Wizard build path is gone.
      Meson is the sole supported build path.
   *  The auto-tuning Wizard is reincarnated as a Python tool
      (`ntl-wizard`) with full parameter parity.  Install with
      `pip install ./tools`.
   *  Every DoConfig option has a Meson equivalent or a documented
      migration; see doc/migration-from-makefile.txt.


